<edge id="christie-prosecuted-charles-kushner" source="n87" target="n8"><data key="e_n">87</data><data key="e_id">christie-prosecuted-charles-kushner</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">prosecution (guilty plea)</data><data key="e_category">pardon/settlement</data><data key="e_label">prosecutes; plea 2004</data><data key="e_date">2004-08-18 ; 2005-03-04</data><data key="e_grade">V</data><data key="e_saiddone"></data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-09 (v3)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-09</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-09-V-powermap-v3-christie-prosecuted-charles-kushner</data><data key="e_source_tier">primary</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">1</data><data key="e_single_source">True</data><data key="e_sources">https://www.justice.gov/archive/tax/usaopress/2004/txdv04kush0818_r.htm ; https://www.justice.gov/archive/tax/usaopress/2005/txdv05kush0304_r.htm</data><data key="e_claim">PROSECUTION: Then-US Attorney Chris Christie announced Charles Kushner's guilty plea (2004-08-18) to 16 false-tax-return counts, retaliating against a cooperating witness (hiring a prostitute to seduce and film his brother-in-law, tape mailed to his sister) and false FEC statements; sentenced to 24 months (2005-03-04). Pardoned by Trump 2020 (existing edge).</data></edge>
<edge id="lunate-affinity" source="n96" target="n36"><data key="e_n">88</data><data key="e_id">lunate-affinity</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">funding (LP stake)</data><data key="e_category">funding</data><data key="e_label">LP ($1.5B w/ QIA 2024)</data><data key="e_date">2024 ; 2026</data><data key="e_grade">V</data><data key="e_saiddone"></data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-09 (v3)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-09</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-09-V-powermap-v3-lunate-affinity</data><data key="e_source_tier">press</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">1</data><data key="e_single_source">True</data><data key="e_sources">https://www.smh.com.au/world/europe/us-russia-talks-on-ukraine-now-involve-an-oil-deal-tied-to-trump-allies-20261004-p612ot.html</data><data key="e_claim">FUNDING: Abu Dhabi's Lunate (a fund Sheikh Tahnoon bin Zayed helps oversee; his Aryam bought 49% of WLF) and QIA added $1.5B to Kushner's Affinity in 2024 (Reuters, per register row); NYT (Oct 2026): Lunate is among Affinity's largest stakeholders, making Tahnoon 'effectively a business partner' of Kushner.</data></edge>
<edge id="khayyat-kushner-albania" source="n95" target="n36"><data key="e_n">89</data><data key="e_id">khayyat-kushner-albania</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">business deal (Albania resort partnership)</data><data key="e_category">business</data><data key="e_label">Albania resort partners 2025-26</data><data key="e_date">2025 - 2026</data><data key="e_grade">V</data><data key="e_saiddone"></data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-09 (v3)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-09</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-09-V-powermap-v3-khayyat-kushner-albania</data><data key="e_source_tier">press</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">1</data><data key="e_single_source">True</data><data key="e_sources">https://www.smh.com.au/world/europe/us-russia-talks-on-ukraine-now-involve-an-oil-deal-tied-to-trump-allies-20261004-p612ot.html</data><data key="e_claim">BUSINESS: Qatari brothers Moutaz and Ramez Al-Khayyat (attended Trump's 2025 inauguration) partner with Jared Kushner and Ivanka Trump to finance a multibillion-dollar luxury resort in southern Albania; Ramez met Ivanka in Albania in 2026 (NYT). They are a major equity holder in the Boehly-led Lukoil bid.</data></edge>
