<edge id="trump-putin-call-diesel-gl135" source="n0" target="n91"><data key="e_n">94</data><data key="e_id">trump-putin-call-diesel-gl135</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">call + sanctions licence (GL 135)</data><data key="e_category">pardon/settlement</data><data key="e_label">call + diesel GL 135 2026-10-09</data><data key="e_date">2026-10-09</data><data key="e_grade">V</data><data key="e_saiddone"></data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-09 (v3)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-21</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-09-V-powermap-v3-trump-putin-call-diesel-gl135</data><data key="e_source_tier">primary</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">2</data><data key="e_single_source">False</data><data key="e_sources">http://en.kremlin.ru/events/president/news/80960 ; https://www.cnbc.com/2026/10/09/trump-putin-russian-diesel-us-global-markets.html</data><data key="e_claim">CALL + SANCTIONS RELIEF: Trump and Putin spoke 2026-10-09 (Kremlin statement: Russia 'willing to supply oil and petroleum products to the US market'); Treasury's OFAC issued General License 135 the same afternoon, temporarily authorizing Russian-origin diesel sales and imports through Apr 2027. Tonnages (300k t now ... 4M t) are Trump SAID only.</data></edge>
