<edge id="trump-v-irs-weaponization-fund" source="n89" target="n0"><data key="e_n">98</data><data key="e_id">trump-v-irs-weaponization-fund</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">settlement (own government; $1.776B fund; enjoined)</data><data key="e_category">pardon/settlement</data><data key="e_label">settles: $1.776B fund 2026-05 (enjoined)</data><data key="e_date">2026-05-18 ; 2026-06-12</data><data key="e_grade">V</data><data key="e_saiddone"></data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">enjoined</data><data key="e_status_date">2026-06-12</data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-09 (v3)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-06-12</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-09-V-powermap-v3-trump-v-irs-weaponization-fund</data><data key="e_source_tier">primary</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">2</data><data key="e_single_source">False</data><data key="e_sources">https://www.justice.gov/opa/pr/justice-department-announces-anti-weaponization-fund ; https://rollcall.com/2026/06/12/court-extends-block-on-anti-weaponization-fund/</data><data key="e_claim">SETTLEMENT: In Trump v. IRS (plaintiffs Trump, Don Jr., Eric Trump, Trump Org; suit over the tax-return leak, $10B sought), acting AG Todd Blanche's DOJ settled on 2026-05-18 by creating a $1.776B 'Anti-Weaponization Fund' from the Judgment Fund (plaintiffs: apology, no money). Blanche later told Congress it was 'not moving forward'; Judge Brinkema kept it enjoined on 2026-06-12, citing Trump's own statements that he still wanted it.</data></edge>
