<edge id="trump-miran-cea-fed" source="n0" target="n149"><data key="e_n">155</data><data key="e_id">trump-miran-cea-fed</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">appointment (CEA chair -&gt; Fed governor)</data><data key="e_category">appointment</data><data key="e_label">CEA -&gt; Fed 2025-09</data><data key="e_date">2025-03 ; 2025-09-15</data><data key="e_grade">V</data><data key="e_saiddone"></data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-09 (v5)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-09</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v5-V-trump-miran-cea-fed</data><data key="e_source_tier">primary</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">2</data><data key="e_single_source">False</data><data key="e_sources">https://www.cnbc.com/2025/09/15/trump-stephen-miran-federal-reserve-interest-rates.html ; https://www.congress.gov/nomination/119th-congress/19</data><data key="e_claim">APPOINTMENT: Trump's CEA chair Stephen Miran was confirmed 48-47 to the Fed Board Sep 15 2025 while on unpaid leave from the CEA. That dual role drew independence objections.</data></edge>
<edge id="witkoff-park-lane-qia" source="n6" target="n150"><data key="e_n">156</data><data key="e_id">witkoff-park-lane-qia</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">business deal (asset sale, $623M)</data><data key="e_category">funding</data><data key="e_label">sells Park Lane $623M 2023</data><data key="e_date">2023-08</data><data key="e_grade">V</data><data key="e_saiddone"></data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-09 (v5)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-09</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v5-V-witkoff-park-lane-qia</data><data key="e_source_tier">press</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">2</data><data key="e_single_source">False</data><data key="e_sources">https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2023-08-28/manhattan-hotel-once-linked-to-1mdb-scandal-sells-to-qataris ; https://therealdeal.com/new-york/2023/08/28/qia-buys-park-lane-hotel-from-witkoff/</data><data key="e_claim">BUSINESS DEAL: Qatar's sovereign fund QIA bought Witkoff Group's Park Lane Hotel (Central Park South) for ~$623M in Aug 2023, before Witkoff became the Mideast envoy who works with Qatar's PM.</data></edge>
<edge id="stover-approved-maxwell-transfer" source="n152" target="n122"><data key="e_n">157</data><data key="e_id">stover-approved-maxwell-transfer</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">approval (BOP waiver/transfer to FPC Bryan)</data><data key="e_category">business</data><data key="e_label">approves camp transfer 2025-08</data><data key="e_date">2025-08-01 ; confirmed 2026-09</data><data key="e_grade">V</data><data key="e_saiddone"></data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-09 (v6)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-09</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v6-V-stover-approved-maxwell-transfer</data><data key="e_source_tier">press</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">2</data><data key="e_single_source">False</data><data key="e_sources">https://www.themarshallproject.org/2026/09/18/blanche-changes-federal-prison-placements ; https://www.nbcnews.com/news/us-news/texas-federal-prison-camp-bryan-ghislaine-maxwell-was-moved-steps-secu-rcna223464</data><data key="e_claim">APPROVAL: The BOP press office confirmed to The Marshall Project (Sep 2026) that Rick Stover, special assistant to the BOP director, was the 'approving official' for Maxwell's move to FPC Bryan about a week after the Blanche proffer. A former senior BOP official says Maxwell is the only sex offender given such a waiver since 2006. Bondi told the House she had nothing to do with it. Who, if anyone, directed Stover is open (hole).</data></edge>
<edge id="bondi-qatar-jet-memo" source="n136" target="n0"><data key="e_n">158</data><data key="e_id">bondi-qatar-jet-memo</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">legal memo (Qatar 747 gift; OLC-cleared, unreleased)</data><data key="e_category">funding</data><data key="e_label">747 memo 2025-05 (I)</data><data key="e_date">2025-05</data><data key="e_grade">I</data><data key="e_saiddone"></data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-09 (v6)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-12</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v6-I-bondi-qatar-jet-memo</data><data key="e_source_tier">press</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">2</data><data key="e_single_source">False</data><data key="e_sources">https://www.cnn.com/2025/05/14/politics/bondi-justice-department-trump-qatar-747 ; https://americanoversight.org/doj-sued-for-withholding-legal-memo-on-trump-administrations-400-million-jet-gifted-by-qatar/</data><data key="e_claim">MEMO (I): Per a DOJ official (CNN) and NYT/ABC sources, AG Bondi, Qatar's 2019-20 registered agent, signed an OLC-cleared memo, sent to WH Counsel Warrington, finding it lawful for DoD to accept Qatar's 747-8 and later transfer it to Trump's library foundation. The memo itself is unreleased (FOIA suit, Jul 2025), hence I.</data></edge>
<edge id="hegseth-accepts-qatar-747" source="n14" target="n137"><data key="e_n">159</data><data key="e_id">hegseth-accepts-qatar-747</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">acceptance of foreign-government gift (747-8)</data><data key="e_category">funding</data><data key="e_label">accepts 747 2025-05-21</data><data key="e_date">2025-05-21</data><data key="e_grade">V</data><data key="e_saiddone"></data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-09 (v6)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-09</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v6-V-hegseth-accepts-qatar-747</data><data key="e_source_tier">press</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">1</data><data key="e_single_source">True</data><data key="e_sources">https://www.factcheck.org/2025/05/unwrapping-qatars-400-million-winged-gift-to-trump/</data><data key="e_claim">GIFT: Pentagon statement May 21 2025: 'The Secretary of Defense has accepted a Boeing 747 from Qatar' for presidential use (FactCheck.org quoting Parnell). Edge drawn to the Qatar state node.</data></edge>
<edge id="son-trump-100b-pledge" source="n153" target="n0"><data key="e_n">160</data><data key="e_id">son-trump-100b-pledge</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">documented meeting ; investment pledge</data><data key="e_category">contact</data><data key="e_label">$100B pledge 2024-12</data><data key="e_date">2024-12-16 ; 2025-01-21</data><data key="e_grade">V</data><data key="e_saiddone"></data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-09 (v6)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-12</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v6-V-son-trump-100b-pledge</data><data key="e_source_tier">press</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">2</data><data key="e_single_source">False</data><data key="e_sources">https://www.reuters.com/business/finance/softbank-ceo-announce-100-bln-investment-us-during-visit-trump-cnbc-reports-2024-12-16/ ; https://apnews.com/article/donald-trump-softbank-investment-us-8df47668f894b5d922839d98887bbb0e</data><data key="e_claim">MEETING/PLEDGE: Son announced at Mar-a-Lago with Trump (and Lutnick) a $100B US investment over four years (Dec 16 2024). He then chaired Stargate, announced at the WH Jan 21 2025.</data></edge>
<edge id="trump-powell-fed-tour" source="n0" target="n154"><data key="e_n">161</data><data key="e_id">trump-powell-fed-tour</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">pressure campaign ; documented meeting (Fed tour)</data><data key="e_category">contact</data><data key="e_label">Fed tour 2025-07-24</data><data key="e_date">2025-07-24</data><data key="e_grade">V</data><data key="e_saiddone"></data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-09 (v6)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-09</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v6-V-trump-powell-fed-tour</data><data key="e_source_tier">press</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">2</data><data key="e_single_source">False</data><data key="e_sources">https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/remarks-during-tour-the-federal-reserve-system-headquarters-and-exchange-with-reporters ; https://apnews.com/article/trump-federal-reserve-jerome-powell-145b0189a8c7acaab9fcfb097dc376c9</data><data key="e_claim">MEETING: Trump toured the Fed renovation with Powell on Jul 24 2025 and disputed the cost on camera ($3.1B vs Powell's correction). He had called it a possible 'fireable offense', then said firing was not 'necessary'. Powell's chair term ended May 2026; Warsh was nominated.</data></edge>
