<edge id="lauder-greenland-pitch" source="n135" target="n0"><data key="e_n">165</data><data key="e_id">lauder-greenland-pitch</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">advocacy (Greenland purchase idea)</data><data key="e_category">contact</data><data key="e_label">Greenland pitch 2018 (I)</data><data key="e_date">2018 ; 2025-26</data><data key="e_grade">I</data><data key="e_saiddone"></data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-09 (v6)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-09</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v6-I-lauder-greenland-pitch</data><data key="e_source_tier">press</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">2</data><data key="e_single_source">False</data><data key="e_sources">https://www.nytimes.com/2022/09/14/us/politics/trump-greenland.html ; https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/jan/15/ronald-lauder-billionaire-donor-donald-trump-ukraine-greenland</data><data key="e_claim">ADVOCACY (I): Per NYT (Baker/Glasser book, 2022) and Guardian (Jan 2026), Lauder pitched Trump in 2018 on buying Greenland and offered to be a back channel to Denmark. Trump told Bolton a 'really, really experienced businessman' proposed it. The Guardian reports Lauder holds Greenland business interests. Book and anonymous sourcing, hence I.</data></edge>
<edge id="palantir-ice-immigrationos" source="n25" target="n157"><data key="e_n">166</data><data key="e_id">palantir-ice-immigrationos</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">contract ($29.8M ImmigrationOS)</data><data key="e_category">contract</data><data key="e_label">ImmigrationOS $29.8M 2025</data><data key="e_date">2025-04</data><data key="e_grade">V</data><data key="e_saiddone"></data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-09 (v6)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-09</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v6-V-palantir-ice-immigrationos</data><data key="e_source_tier">press</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">2</data><data key="e_single_source">False</data><data key="e_sources">https://www.wired.com/story/ice-palantir-immigrationos/ ; https://www.businessinsider.com/ice-palantir-new-technology-30-million-visa-overstays-self-deportation-2025-4</data><data key="e_claim">CONTRACT: ICE paid Palantir ~$29.8M (modification to an existing contract) to build the 'ImmigrationOS' prototype by Sep 25 2025, for deportation targeting and self-deportation tracking (contract doc via Wired).</data></edge>
