<edge id="barrack-smith-syria-sanctions" source="n80" target="n106"><data key="e_n">175</data><data key="e_id">barrack-smith-syria-sanctions</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">joint official action (Syria sanctions removal briefing)</data><data key="e_category">pardon/settlement</data><data key="e_label">joint Syria briefing 2025-06</data><data key="e_date">2025-06-30</data><data key="e_grade">V</data><data key="e_saiddone"></data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-09 (v7)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-09</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v7-V-barrack-smith-syria-sanctions</data><data key="e_source_tier">primary</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">1</data><data key="e_single_source">True</data><data key="e_sources">https://www.state.gov/releases/office-of-the-spokesperson/2025/06/u-s-ambassador-to-turkiye-and-special-envoy-for-syria-thomas-barrack-and-acting-under-secretary-brad-smith-terrorism-and-financial-intelligence-treasury</data><data key="e_claim">JOINT ACTION: Barrack and Brad Smith (then acting Treasury TFI under secretary) briefed jointly on the record Jun 30 2025 on removing Syria sanctions (State transcript).</data></edge>
<edge id="altman-trump-wh" source="n163" target="n0"><data key="e_n">176</data><data key="e_id">altman-trump-wh</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">documented meetings (WH Stargate; WH tech dinner)</data><data key="e_category">contact</data><data key="e_label">WH 2025-01 + 2025-09</data><data key="e_date">2025-01-21 ; 2025-09-04</data><data key="e_grade">V</data><data key="e_saiddone"></data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-09 (v7)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-09</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v7-V-altman-trump-wh</data><data key="e_source_tier">primary</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">2</data><data key="e_single_source">False</data><data key="e_sources">https://www.whitehouse.gov/releases/2025/09/president-trump-tech-leaders-unite-american-ai-dominance/ ; https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/remarks-artificial-intelligence-infrastructure-development-and-exchange-with-reporters</data><data key="e_claim">MEETINGS: Altman stood with Trump at the Jan 21 2025 Stargate announcement and attended the Sep 4 2025 WH tech dinner ('Thank you for being such a pro-business, pro-innovation President'; WH release).</data></edge>
<edge id="openai-g42-stargate-uae" source="n163" target="n164"><data key="e_n">177</data><data key="e_id">openai-g42-stargate-uae</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">business deal (Stargate UAE, 1GW)</data><data key="e_category">business</data><data key="e_label">Stargate UAE 2025-05</data><data key="e_date">2025-05-22</data><data key="e_grade">V</data><data key="e_saiddone"></data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-09 (v7)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-09</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v7-V-openai-g42-stargate-uae</data><data key="e_source_tier">primary</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">2</data><data key="e_single_source">False</data><data key="e_sources">https://openai.com/index/introducing-stargate-uae/ ; https://www.g42.ai/resources/news/global-tech-alliance-launches-stargate-uae</data><data key="e_claim">DEAL: OpenAI with G42, Oracle, NVIDIA, Cisco and SoftBank launched Stargate UAE (1GW Abu Dhabi cluster, 200MW in 2026) on the UAE-US AI Campus announced with MBZ and Trump the week before; 'developed in close coordination with the U.S. government' (OpenAI; G42).</data></edge>
<edge id="vought-powell-letter" source="n165" target="n154"><data key="e_n">178</data><data key="e_id">vought-powell-letter</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">official letter (pressure campaign)</data><data key="e_category">business</data><data key="e_label">letter 2025-07-10</data><data key="e_date">2025-07-10 ; 2025-07-17</data><data key="e_grade">V</data><data key="e_saiddone"></data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-09 (v7)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-09</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v7-V-vought-powell-letter</data><data key="e_source_tier">primary</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">2</data><data key="e_single_source">False</data><data key="e_sources">https://www.federalreserve.gov/foia/files/vought-letter-20250717.pdf ; https://www.cnbc.com/2025/07/17/powell-trump-vought-renovation.html</data><data key="e_claim">LETTER: OMB Director Vought wrote Powell Jul 10 2025 ('The President is extremely troubled...', 'ostentatious overhaul'; 7-day deadline). Powell replied Jul 17 (Fed FOIA PDF).</data></edge>
<edge id="palantir-maven-1-3b" source="n25" target="n14"><data key="e_n">179</data><data key="e_id">palantir-maven-1-3b</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">contract (Maven Smart System ceiling to ~$1.3B)</data><data key="e_category">contract</data><data key="e_label">Maven ceiling ~$1.3B 2025-05</data><data key="e_date">2025-05-21</data><data key="e_grade">V</data><data key="e_saiddone"></data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-09 (v7)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-09</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v7-V-palantir-maven-1-3b</data><data key="e_source_tier">primary</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">2</data><data key="e_single_source">False</data><data key="e_sources">https://www.war.gov/News/Contracts/Contract/Article/4194643/contracts-for-may-21-2025/ ; https://defensescoop.com/2025/05/23/dod-palantir-maven-smart-system-contract-increase/</data><data key="e_claim">CONTRACT: DoD raised Palantir's Maven Smart System ceiling from $480M to ~$1.3B (+$795M modification, through May 2029) per the May 21 2025 contract announcements, under Hegseth's department.</data></edge>
<edge id="smith-gl131-series-lukoil" source="n106" target="n92"><data key="e_n">180</data><data key="e_id">smith-gl131-series-lukoil</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">licenses (GL 131I/131J: Lukoil sale talks)</data><data key="e_category">business</data><data key="e_label">GL 131I/J 2026-08/09</data><data key="e_date">2026-08-20 ; 2026-09-18</data><data key="e_grade">V</data><data key="e_saiddone"></data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-09 (v8)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-21</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v8-V-smith-gl131-series-lukoil</data><data key="e_source_tier">primary</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">1</data><data key="e_single_source">True</data><data key="e_sources">https://ofac.treasury.gov/media/936951/download?inline= ; https://ofac.treasury.gov/media/936731/download ; https://ofac.treasury.gov/faqs/1224</data><data key="e_claim">LICENSES: Director Smith digitally signed GL 131I (2026-08-20 08:38:56 ET, to Sep 19) and GL 131J (2026-09-18 08:32:01 ET, to Oct 22 2026). Both authorize only contingent contracts for the sale of Lukoil International GmbH. OFAC FAQ 1224: any sale license will require cutting ties with Lukoil, blocking proceeds in a US account and 'no windfall'/up-front value to Lukoil.</data></edge>
<edge id="tahnoon-chairs-g42" source="n116" target="n164"><data key="e_n">181</data><data key="e_id">tahnoon-chairs-g42</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">board (chairman)</data><data key="e_category">employment</data><data key="e_label">chairman</data><data key="e_date">2024 - present</data><data key="e_grade">V</data><data key="e_saiddone"></data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-09 (v8)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-09</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v8-V-tahnoon-chairs-g42</data><data key="e_source_tier">primary</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">2</data><data key="e_single_source">False</data><data key="e_sources">https://news.microsoft.com/source/2024/04/16/microsoft-invests-1-5-billion-in-abu-dhabis-g42-to-accelerate-ai-development-and-global-expansion/ ; https://apnews.com/article/microsoft-g42-ai-uae-abu-dhabi-jais-8a9e3f9840a10f151e2421efb195c9b6</data><data key="e_claim">BOARD: Tahnoon is Chairman of G42 (Microsoft release on its $1.5B G42 stake, Apr 16 2024; Microsoft's Brad Smith, not OFAC's, joined the G42 board). This links Stargate UAE (OpenAI/Oracle/G42) to Tahnoon.</data></edge>
<edge id="tahnoon-chairs-ihc" source="n116" target="n166"><data key="e_n">182</data><data key="e_id">tahnoon-chairs-ihc</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">board (chairman)</data><data key="e_category">employment</data><data key="e_label">chairman</data><data key="e_date">- present</data><data key="e_grade">V</data><data key="e_saiddone"></data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-09 (v8)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-09</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v8-V-tahnoon-chairs-ihc</data><data key="e_source_tier">primary</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">1</data><data key="e_single_source">True</data><data key="e_sources">https://apigateway.adx.ae/adx/cdn/1.0/content/download/4700060 ; https://apigateway.adx.ae/adx/cdn/1.0/content/download/4267777</data><data key="e_claim">BOARD: Tahnoon is Chairman of IHC (ADX FY2025 results release, Feb 13 2026; ultimate parent Royal Group Holding per 2024 directors' report).</data></edge>
<edge id="ihc-boehly-lukoil-bid" source="n166" target="n92"><data key="e_n">183</data><data key="e_id">ihc-boehly-lukoil-bid</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">consortium member (bid, pending)</data><data key="e_category">business</data><data key="e_label">in Boehly bid (I)</data><data key="e_date">2026-09 - 2026-10</data><data key="e_grade">I</data><data key="e_saiddone"></data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-09 (v8)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-09</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v8-I-ihc-boehly-lukoil-bid</data><data key="e_source_tier">press</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">2</data><data key="e_single_source">False</data><data key="e_sources">https://www.smh.com.au/world/europe/us-russia-talks-on-ukraine-now-involve-an-oil-deal-tied-to-trump-allies-20261004-p612ot.html ; https://www.oilandgasmiddleeast.com/news/boehly-led-consortium-backed-by-us-and-gulf-investors-bids-for-lukoils-international-assets</data><data key="e_claim">BID (I): NYT (via SMH) names IHC, 'overseen by' Tahnoon, with Boehly, the US DFC and the Al-Khayyats' Power International in the Lukoil bid. FT (via secondary outlets) reports DFC ~15% equity. No filing seen, hence I.</data></edge>
<edge id="dfc-boehly-lukoil-bid" source="n167" target="n92"><data key="e_n">184</data><data key="e_id">dfc-boehly-lukoil-bid</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">co-investor (bid, ~15% equity reported)</data><data key="e_category">business</data><data key="e_label">~15% co-invest (I)</data><data key="e_date">2026-09</data><data key="e_grade">I</data><data key="e_saiddone"></data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-09 (v8)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-09</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v8-I-dfc-boehly-lukoil-bid</data><data key="e_source_tier">press</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">2</data><data key="e_single_source">False</data><data key="e_sources">https://www.smh.com.au/world/europe/us-russia-talks-on-ukraine-now-involve-an-oil-deal-tied-to-trump-allies-20261004-p612ot.html ; https://www.oilandgasmiddleeast.com/news/boehly-led-consortium-backed-by-us-and-gulf-investors-bids-for-lukoils-international-assets</data><data key="e_claim">CO-INVEST (I): The US International Development Finance Corp. is reported (FT via secondary outlets; NYT) as an equity co-investor (~15%) in the Boehly-led bid. A senior official told NYT that Witkoff and Kushner helped negotiate 'a substantial upfront payment and profits interest for the United States'. No DFC board record seen.</data></edge>
<edge id="trump-sharaa-riyadh-wh" source="n0" target="n162"><data key="e_n">185</data><data key="e_id">trump-sharaa-riyadh-wh</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">documented meetings (Riyadh; White House)</data><data key="e_category">contact</data><data key="e_label">Riyadh 2025-05; WH 2025-11</data><data key="e_date">2025-05-14 ; 2025-11-10</data><data key="e_grade">V</data><data key="e_saiddone"></data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-09 (v8)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-09</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v8-V-trump-sharaa-riyadh-wh</data><data key="e_source_tier">press</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">2</data><data key="e_single_source">False</data><data key="e_sources">https://apnews.com/article/trump-syria-saudi-arabia-sharaa-assad-sanctions-bb208f25cfedecd6446fd1626012c0fb ; https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/trump-meet-sharaa-white-house-capping-major-turnaround-syria-2025-11-10/</data><data key="e_claim">MEETINGS: Trump met al-Sharaa in Riyadh on May 14 2025, right after announcing all Syria sanctions would be lifted, and hosted him at the White House on Nov 10 2025 (first Syrian president). OUTCOME: Syria joins the anti-ISIS coalition; Treasury sanctions action announced the same day.</data></edge>
<edge id="trump-putin-alaska-2025" source="n0" target="n91"><data key="e_n">186</data><data key="e_id">trump-putin-alaska-2025</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">documented meeting (Anchorage summit)</data><data key="e_category">contact</data><data key="e_label">Anchorage 2025-08-15</data><data key="e_date">2025-08-15</data><data key="e_grade">V</data><data key="e_saiddone"></data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-09 (v8)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-09</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v8-V-trump-putin-alaska-2025</data><data key="e_source_tier">primary</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">2</data><data key="e_single_source">False</data><data key="e_sources">http://en.kremlin.ru/events/president/news/77791 ; https://www.adn.com/politics/2025/08/15/all-eyes-are-on-anchorage-as-trump-putin-talks-begin/</data><data key="e_claim">SUMMIT: Trump and Putin met at JB Elmendorf-Richardson Aug 15 2025, three-on-three with Rubio and Witkoff / Lavrov and Ushakov (Kremlin). The wider delegations included Bessent, Lutnick, Hegseth and Ratcliffe; on the Russian side Belousov, Siluanov and Dmitriev. OUTCOME: no deal.</data></edge>
<edge id="rubio-lavrov-repeat" source="n105" target="n101"><data key="e_n">187</data><data key="e_id">rubio-lavrov-repeat</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">documented meetings (repeat)</data><data key="e_category">contact</data><data key="e_label">Jul + Aug 2025</data><data key="e_date">2025-02-18 ; 2025-07 ; 2025-08-15</data><data key="e_grade">V</data><data key="e_saiddone"></data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-09 (v8)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-09</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v8-V-rubio-lavrov-repeat</data><data key="e_source_tier">primary</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">2</data><data key="e_single_source">False</data><data key="e_sources">http://en.kremlin.ru/events/president/news/77791 ; https://thehill.com/homenews/administration/5453844-peace-talks-ukraine-russia/</data><data key="e_claim">REPEAT CONTACT: After Riyadh, Rubio met Lavrov in early July 2025 (The Hill) and sat across from him in the Anchorage three-on-three Aug 15 2025 (Kremlin).</data></edge>
<edge id="dmitriev-alaska-delegation" source="n99" target="n168"><data key="e_n">188</data><data key="e_id">dmitriev-alaska-delegation</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">same summit delegation (economic track)</data><data key="e_category">business</data><data key="e_label">Anchorage delegations (I)</data><data key="e_date">2025-08-15</data><data key="e_grade">I</data><data key="e_saiddone"></data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-09 (v8)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-09</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v8-I-dmitriev-alaska-delegation</data><data key="e_source_tier">press</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">2</data><data key="e_single_source">False</data><data key="e_sources">https://www.adn.com/politics/2025/08/15/all-eyes-are-on-anchorage-as-trump-putin-talks-begin/ ; https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/live-updates-trump-to-meet-with-putin-in-alaska</data><data key="e_claim">PRESENCE (I): Dmitriev was in Putin's Anchorage delegation; Bessent and Lutnick were in Trump's (ADN; PBS citing Ushakov). A direct Dmitriev-Bessent/Lutnick meeting there is not documented, hence I.</data></edge>
<edge id="lutnick-epstein-neighbours-lsj-lunch-2012" source="n2" target="n70"><data key="e_n">189</data><data key="e_id">lutnick-epstein-neighbours-lsj-lunch-2012</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">documented meeting (Little St. James lunch) ; neighbours (E 71st St)</data><data key="e_category">contact</data><data key="e_label">island lunch 2012</data><data key="e_date">2005 ; 2012-12-23</data><data key="e_grade">V</data><data key="e_saiddone">BOTH</data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-09 (v9)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-09</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v9-V-lutnick-epstein-neighbours-lsj-lunch-2012</data><data key="e_source_tier">primary</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">3</data><data key="e_single_source">False</data><data key="e_sources">https://oversight.house.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/Lutnick-Transcript.pdf ; https://abcnews.com/Politics/lutnick-called-interactions-epstein-meaningless-inconsequential-transcript/story?id=132938658 ; https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/politics-news/howard-lutnick-congressional-showdown-epstein-files-island-visit-rcna343523</data><data key="e_claim">DONE: Lutnick lived next door to Epstein on E 71st St and, by his own sworn account to House Oversight (transcribed interview May 6 2026, transcript released May 2026), visited Little St. James on Dec 23 2012 for an hour-long lunch with his wife, four children, another family and staff; Epstein's assistant emailed the next day 'Nice seeing you' (NBC, from the files). SAID: Lutnick calls his three in-person contacts (2005 coffee, the 2012 lunch, a later scaffolding chat) 'meaningless and inconsequential' and says Epstein's staff arranged the visit. Register: vault-2012-12-19-lutnick-lsj-lunch-email.</data></edge>
<edge id="lutnick-epstein-adfin-2012" source="n2" target="n70"><data key="e_n">190</data><data key="e_id">lutnick-epstein-adfin-2012</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">business deal (same AdFin Series A purchase agreement)</data><data key="e_category">business</data><data key="e_label">AdFin co-investors 2012</data><data key="e_date">2012-12-28</data><data key="e_grade">V</data><data key="e_saiddone">DONE</data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-09 (v9)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-09</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v9-V-lutnick-epstein-adfin-2012</data><data key="e_source_tier">press</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">3</data><data key="e_single_source">False</data><data key="e_sources">https://www.cbsnews.com/news/howard-lutnick-jeffrey-epstein-in-business-together/ ; https://tommycarstensen.com/epstein/data/documents/set9/00289/EFTA00289560.html ; https://www.npr.org/2026/05/06/nx-s1-5814081/howard-lutnick-epstein-files-house-oversight-committee</data><data key="e_claim">DONE: Epstein (for Southern Trust Company) and Lutnick (for CVAFH I LLC) signed the same AdFin Solutions Series A preferred-stock purchase agreement dated Dec 28 2012, five days after the island lunch; their stakes were set for later 2013 closings (CBS; EFTA00289560). Lutnick communicated with Epstein through Epstein's assistant as late as 2018 (NPR). Two acts, same month: the lunch and the deal are separate edges; no claim the lunch caused the deal.</data></edge>
<edge id="hoffman-epstein-baume-2015" source="n169" target="n70"><data key="e_n">191</data><data key="e_id">hoffman-epstein-baume-2015</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">documented meeting (hosted dinner, Baume, Palo Alto)</data><data key="e_category">contact</data><data key="e_label">hosted dinner 2015</data><data key="e_date">2015-08-02</data><data key="e_grade">V</data><data key="e_saiddone">DONE</data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-09 (v9)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-09</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v9-V-hoffman-epstein-baume-2015</data><data key="e_source_tier">press</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">3</data><data key="e_single_source">False</data><data key="e_sources">https://tommycarstensen.com/epstein/data/documents/set10/02073/EFTA02073963.html ; https://www.epsteinscan.org/document/1221465 ; https://www.nbcnews.com/tech/tech-news/jeffrey-epstein-files-reveal-deep-tech-ties-musk-gates-rcna257092</data><data key="e_claim">DONE: Reid Hoffman's office (EA Saida Sapieva, LinkedIn &amp; Greylock) organised the Aug 2 2015 bought-out dinner at Baume, Palo Alto, for MIT's Ed Boyden, and Epstein's office confirmed he 'most definitely would like to participate'; the attendee list includes Epstein, Hoffman, Thiel, Musk, Zuckerberg, Chan and Joi Ito (EFTA02073963, EFTA02074074). Epstein's assistant called it 'Reid Hoffman/Peter Thiel's dinner party'. Separately, WSJ (2023, per NBC) reported Hoffman visited Epstein's island and introduced Epstein to Thiel. Register: grokbot-2026-10-09-I-farnsjennifer-2108740350491955289-baume-rykov-aug2015.</data></edge>
<edge id="zuckerberg-epstein-baume-2015" source="n63" target="n70"><data key="e_n">192</data><data key="e_id">zuckerberg-epstein-baume-2015</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">documented meeting (same dinner; contact-details request)</data><data key="e_category">contact</data><data key="e_label">met at dinner 2015</data><data key="e_date">2015-08-02 ; 2015-08-05</data><data key="e_grade">V</data><data key="e_saiddone">BOTH</data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-09 (v9)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-09</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v9-V-zuckerberg-epstein-baume-2015</data><data key="e_source_tier">primary</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">3</data><data key="e_single_source">False</data><data key="e_sources">https://www.justice.gov/epstein/files/DataSet%2010/EFTA02074070.pdf ; https://epsteinexposed.com/documents/efta-efta02074070 ; https://www.nbcnews.com/tech/tech-news/jeffrey-epstein-files-reveal-deep-tech-ties-musk-gates-rcna257092</data><data key="e_claim">DONE: Zuckerberg (with Priscilla Chan) is on the Baume attendee list with Epstein (Aug 2 2015), and on Aug 5 Epstein's assistant wrote to Zuckerberg's chief of staff Andrea Besmehn that 'Mark requested Jeffrey send his contact details to him' and passed them on; Besmehn replied 'Noted, with thanks' (EFTA02074070). SAID: Meta says Zuckerberg 'met Epstein in passing one time' and did not communicate with him again (2019 and 2026 statements, NBC). Only the contact swap is one-to-one; no later contact is documented.</data></edge>
<edge id="musk-epstein-baume-2015" source="n32" target="n70"><data key="e_n">193</data><data key="e_id">musk-epstein-baume-2015</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">same event (attendee list, Baume dinner)</data><data key="e_category">business</data><data key="e_label">same dinner 2015</data><data key="e_date">2015-08-02</data><data key="e_grade">V</data><data key="e_saiddone">DONE</data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-09 (v9)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-09</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v9-V-musk-epstein-baume-2015</data><data key="e_source_tier">reference</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">2</data><data key="e_single_source">False</data><data key="e_sources">https://www.epsteinscan.org/document/1221465 ; https://tommycarstensen.com/epstein/data/documents/set10/02073/EFTA02073963.html</data><data key="e_claim">DONE: Elon Musk is listed as an attendee of the Aug 2 2015 Baume dinner with Epstein in the reconfirmation email from Reid Hoffman's office (EFTA02074074) and the Jul 31 confirmation (EFTA02073963). Attendance only: no one-to-one Musk-Epstein exchange from this dinner is in these documents.</data></edge>
<edge id="rubio-icc-entity-sanctions-2026" source="n105" target="n170"><data key="e_n">194</data><data key="e_id">rubio-icc-entity-sanctions-2026</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">sanctions designation (ICC itself, E.O. 14203; SDN list)</data><data key="e_category">pardon/settlement</data><data key="e_label">sanctions ICC 2026</data><data key="e_date">2026-10-09</data><data key="e_grade">V</data><data key="e_saiddone">BOTH</data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-09 (v9)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-09</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v9-V-rubio-icc-entity-sanctions-2026</data><data key="e_source_tier">primary</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">3</data><data key="e_single_source">False</data><data key="e_sources">https://www.state.gov/releases/office-of-the-spokesman/2026/10/imposing-sanctions-on-the-international-criminal-court/ ; https://apnews.com/article/us-icc-trump-rubio-4ea3555403e3c695d8f81dc473515d9b ; https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/10/9/us-sanctions-international-criminal-court-itself-in-latest-escalation</data><data key="e_claim">DONE: State (Rubio) designated the International Criminal Court itself under E.O. 14203 on Oct 9 2026 (full blocking; OFAC wind-down GLs 13-16). SAID: Rubio, 'Either the ICC will end its threats, or we will end the ICC.' Sequence only: it came hours after ex-ICC judge Navi Pillay won the Nobel Peace Prize; State says the designation had been deferred for over a year. Register: grokbot-2026-10-09-V-statedept-icc-entity-sanctions-hours-after-pillay-nobel.</data></edge>
<edge id="trump-zacharia-press-secretary" source="n0" target="n171"><data key="e_n">195</data><data key="e_id">trump-zacharia-press-secretary</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">appointment (White House press secretary)</data><data key="e_category">appointment</data><data key="e_label">press sec. 2026</data><data key="e_date">2026-10-09</data><data key="e_grade">V</data><data key="e_saiddone">DONE</data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">ended</data><data key="e_status_date">2026-10-23</data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-09 (v9)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-23</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v9-V-trump-zacharia-press-secretary</data><data key="e_source_tier">press</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">2</data><data key="e_single_source">False</data><data key="e_sources">https://apnews.com/article/trump-white-house-press-secretary-katie-zacharia-aaabf8627035da9bc4cd44173f22e02e ; https://www.politico.com/news/2026/10/09/white-house-offers-katie-zacharia-white-house-press-secretary-job-01114597</data><data key="e_claim">DONE: Trump announced on Truth Social on Oct 9 2026 that Katie Zacharia will succeed Karoline Leavitt as White House press secretary; per CNN she was not under consideration a week earlier and Trump sought Leavitt's counsel first.</data></edge>
