<edge id="epstein-summers-treasury-nov2016" source="n70" target="n72"><data key="e_n">201</data><data key="e_id">epstein-summers-treasury-nov2016</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">documented email (treasury-secretary suggestions, Trump transition)</data><data key="e_category">business</data><data key="e_label">treasury picks email 2016</data><data key="e_date">2016-11-27</data><data key="e_grade">V</data><data key="e_saiddone">BOTH</data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-12 (v10)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-12</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-12-powermap-v10-V-epstein-summers-treasury-nov2016</data><data key="e_source_tier">primary</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">2</data><data key="e_single_source">False</data><data key="e_sources">https://www.justice.gov/epstein/files/DataSet%2011/EFTA02669281.pdf ; https://tommycarstensen.com/epstein/data/documents/set11/02669/EFTA02669281.html</data><data key="e_claim">DONE: DOJ doc EFTA02669281 (Dataset 11) exists. SAID (email content): Nov 27 2016 Epstein asks Summers 'do you have any suggestions for treasury?' (19 days after the 2016 election); Summers replies with candidates including Romney, Tony James, Larry Fink, Fred Smith, Peter Thiel, Jeff Immelt, Jamie Dimon; Epstein rates them (e.g. 'Peter Thiel austistic, no global sense'). Distinct from epstein-summers-apr2016 (digital-currency thread). No claim Summers caused any later appointment. Register: grokbot-2026-10-11-V-hannibal-2109367247613366555-epstein-summers-treasury-picks-2016.</data></edge>
