<edge id="lutnick-khashoggi-pierre-deal" source="n2" target="n188"><data key="e_n">215</data><data key="e_id">lutnick-khashoggi-pierre-deal</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">business deal (found buyer, helped structure $2B Pierre bid; terminated)</data><data key="e_category">funding</data><data key="e_label">Pierre $2B bid (dead 10-13)</data><data key="e_date">2024-05 intro ; 2026-10-13 terminated</data><data key="e_grade">V</data><data key="e_saiddone">DONE</data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">ended</data><data key="e_status_date">2026-10-13</data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-14 (v12)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-15</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-14-powermap-v12-V-lutnick-khashoggi-pierre-deal</data><data key="e_source_tier">press</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">1</data><data key="e_single_source">True</data><data key="e_sources">https://dnyuz.com/2026/10/14/battle-over-the-pierre-ends-in-defeat-for-the-buyer-pushed-by-lutnick/</data><data key="e_claim">DONE business deal: NYT (Oct 14 2026) says Commerce Secretary Lutnick, who owns the Pierre penthouse, found Saudi investor Motasem Khashoggi (introduced May 2024 via WhatsApp), met him in London with Dorchester Collection (Brunei-owned) president Christopher Cowdray, and helped craft his $2B bid via Sabre Park Avenue LLC. Records show Lutnick would have netted ~$60M on his unit and Newmark (run by two of his sons) a $30M adviser fee. Lutnick offered Khashoggi's son a BGC internship (taken, per Khashoggi) and turned on disappearing messages after his Dec 2024 nomination. The co-op terminated the deal after the $100M deposit missed the Oct 13 2026 5pm deadline. Lutnick declined comment. Register: grokbot-2026-10-14-V-shachtman-pierre-saudi-deal-dead.</data></edge>
