<edge id="trump-herrera-velutini-pardon-2026" source="n0" target="n238"><data key="e_n">270</data><data key="e_id">trump-herrera-velutini-pardon-2026</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">pardon (full and unconditional, Jan 2026; co-defendants Wanda Vazquez Garced and Mark Rossini pardoned at the same time)</data><data key="e_category">pardon/settlement</data><data key="e_label">pardon (Jan 2026)</data><data key="e_date">2026-01-15</data><data key="e_grade">V</data><data key="e_saiddone">DONE</data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-20 (v16)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-20</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-20-powermap-v16-V-trump-herrera-velutini-pardon-2026</data><data key="e_source_tier">primary</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">2</data><data key="e_single_source">False</data><data key="e_sources">https://www.justice.gov/pardon/clemency-grants-president-donald-j-trump-2025-present ; https://dnyuz.com/2026/10/20/a-billionaire-wanted-a-trump-pardon-his-family-gave-alina-habba-a-50-million-deal/</data><data key="e_claim">DONE (DOJ Office of the Pardon Attorney list): Julio M. Herrera Velutini (D. Puerto Rico; conspiracy, federal program bribery, honest services wire fraud as listed on the warrant) was pardoned, along with ex-Gov. Wanda Vazquez Garced and ex-FBI agent Mark Rossini, before their misdemeanor sentencings (NYT: Jan 15 2026, amended five days later). His lawyer Christopher Kise (ex-Trump legal team) and Ballard Partners (USD 600K Q4 2025 LDA, per CLC) worked the clemency push. WH SAID the review ran through WH Counsel and DOJ.</data></edge>
<edge id="herrera-velutini-isabela-herrera-family" source="n238" target="n239"><data key="e_n">271</data><data key="e_id">herrera-velutini-isabela-herrera-family</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">family (father - daughter; she leads the family office Banvelca since Jul 2026)</data><data key="e_category">family</data><data key="e_label">father - daughter</data><data key="e_date">lifelong</data><data key="e_grade">V</data><data key="e_saiddone">DONE</data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-20 (v16)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-20</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-20-powermap-v16-V-herrera-velutini-isabela-herrera-family</data><data key="e_source_tier">press</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">1</data><data key="e_single_source">True</data><data key="e_sources">https://dnyuz.com/2026/10/20/a-billionaire-wanted-a-trump-pardon-his-family-gave-alina-habba-a-50-million-deal/</data><data key="e_claim">DONE (NYT Oct 20 2026): Isabela Herrera, 27, an American citizen, is Julio Herrera Velutini's daughter; in July 2026 Banvelca, the family office since 1781, announced she was taking over its leadership.</data></edge>
<edge id="isabela-herrera-concord-habba-50m" source="n239" target="n189"><data key="e_n">272</data><data key="e_id">isabela-herrera-concord-habba-50m</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">employment (general counsel of Concord Partners; $10M/yr for 4 years + bonuses, &gt;$50M guaranteed; began Jan 1 2026 while Habba was a DOJ special government employee and senior adviser to AG Bondi)</data><data key="e_category">funding</data><data key="e_label">GC contract &gt;$50M / 4 yrs</data><data key="e_date">2025-10 (deal) / 2026-01-01 (start) - present</data><data key="e_grade">V</data><data key="e_saiddone">BOTH</data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-20 (v16)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-22</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-20-powermap-v16-V-isabela-herrera-concord-habba-50m</data><data key="e_source_tier">press</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">3</data><data key="e_single_source">False</data><data key="e_sources">https://dnyuz.com/2026/10/20/a-billionaire-wanted-a-trump-pardon-his-family-gave-alina-habba-a-50-million-deal/ ; https://www.mediaite.com/crime/billionaire-scored-trump-pardon-after-50-million-deal-with-alina-habba/ ; https://www.elnuevodia.com/corresponsalias/washington-dc/notas/herrera-velutini-consiguio-el-indulto-de-trump-despues-de-un-contrato-de-50-millones-a-una-funcionaria-de-justicia-federal/</data><data key="e_claim">DONE (NYT Oct 20 2026, interviews + documents): the Herrera family hired Alina Habba as general counsel of Concord Partners, a company Isabela Herrera registered in Florida in late Oct 2025, at $10M a year for four years plus bonuses (more than $50M guaranteed). Habba finalized the deal days after registration and started Jan 1 2026 while still a senior adviser to AG Bondi (office at DOJ, Marshals detail). Weeks later Trump pardoned Herrera Velutini: SEQUENCE, no cause shown. SAID: Habba denies any role in the pardon and says DOJ approved the outside job; DOJ SAID she 'did not speak to anyone about a pardon'; a WH official SAID she had nothing to do with it. People familiar with the contract SAID they believed she was hired to help with the pardon push (unnamed).</data></edge>
<edge id="isabela-herrera-maga-inc-3-5m" source="n239" target="n236"><data key="e_n">273</data><data key="e_id">isabela-herrera-maga-inc-3-5m</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">funding (donations $2.5M Dec 31 2024 + $1M Jul 22 2025; CLC FEC complaint alleges a straw-donor/foreign-national source)</data><data key="e_category">funding</data><data key="e_label">$3.5M (2024-25)</data><data key="e_date">2024-12-31 / 2025-07-22</data><data key="e_grade">V</data><data key="e_saiddone">DONE</data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-20 (v16)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-20</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-20-powermap-v16-V-isabela-herrera-maga-inc-3-5m</data><data key="e_source_tier">primary</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">3</data><data key="e_single_source">False</data><data key="e_sources">https://docquery.fec.gov/cgi-bin/fecimg/?202501319752674491 ; https://docquery.fec.gov/cgi-bin/fecimg/?202601029793901866 ; https://dnyuz.com/2026/10/20/a-billionaire-wanted-a-trump-pardon-his-family-gave-alina-habba-a-50-million-deal/ ; https://www.lawcommentary.com/articles/trump-pardon-alina-habba-50-million-deal</data><data key="e_claim">DONE (FEC Schedule A, MAGA Inc. C00892471): HERRERA, ISABELA $2,500,000 on 2024-12-31 and $1,000,000 on 2025-07-22. Her prior federal giving was $20 (CLC). SAID (Campaign Legal Center FEC complaint, Feb 17 2026; interested watchdog): the money may have come from her father, a Venezuelan national, which would be a foreign-national/straw-donor violation; no FEC finding yet. WaPo (per Law Commentary): she pledged $2.5M to the White House ballroom on Sep 23 2025 and paid $835,000 on Oct 14 2025. Donations, then pardon (Jan 2026), is a sequence.</data></edge>
<edge id="grenell-fix-california-zacharia" source="n191" target="n171"><data key="e_n">274</data><data key="e_id">grenell-fix-california-zacharia</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">employment (Zacharia listed as general counsel of Grenell's nonprofit Fix California, Jan 2024 - Mar 2025; IRS filings show $27,367 in fundraising commissions to her in 2024, no salary)</data><data key="e_category">funding</data><data key="e_label">Fix California GC (2024-25)</data><data key="e_date">2024-01 - 2025-03</data><data key="e_grade">V</data><data key="e_saiddone">BOTH</data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-20 (v16)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-20</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-20-powermap-v16-V-grenell-fix-california-zacharia</data><data key="e_source_tier">press</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">3</data><data key="e_single_source">False</data><data key="e_sources">https://www.telegraph.co.uk/us/news/2026/10/14/white-house-kennedy-centre-missing-1m/ ; https://san.com/wp-content/uploads/securepdfs/2026/10/cfa-ca-bar-katie-zacharia.pdf ; https://linkedin.com/in/katie-zacharia</data><data key="e_claim">DONE/SAID: Zacharia's own LinkedIn listed her as full-time General Counsel of Fix California, the California nonprofit Grenell runs, Jan 2024 - Mar 2025 (she removed it by Oct 14 2026); the organization's IRS filings show no salary to her but $27,367 in fundraising commissions in 2024 (Campaign for Accountability State Bar complaint, an interested complainant). Telegraph (Oct 14 2026): Grenell runs a California nonprofit that until recently employed Zacharia. Grenell headed the Kennedy Center and now faces the WH Counsel review over the Mildon gift; Zacharia was named press secretary Oct 9 and was out Oct 16.</data></edge>
<edge id="uk-mod-saudi-defensive-air-2026" source="n240" target="n241"><data key="e_n">275</data><data key="e_id">uk-mod-saudi-defensive-air-2026</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">military support (RAF Typhoon defensive counter-air over Saudi cities, A400M, advisers; extended air-to-air refuelling for Saudi operations incl. degrading Houthi targets)</data><data key="e_category">business</data><data key="e_label">RAF Typhoons + tanking (announced Oct 20 2026)</data><data key="e_date">2026-10-20</data><data key="e_grade">V</data><data key="e_saiddone">SAID</data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-20 (v16)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-20</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-20-powermap-v16-V-uk-mod-saudi-defensive-air-2026</data><data key="e_source_tier">primary</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">2</data><data key="e_single_source">False</data><data key="e_sources">https://www.gov.uk/government/news/operational-update-20-october-uk-military-support-to-the-kingdom-of-saudi-arabia ; https://apnews.com/article/uk-air-patrols-saudi-houthis-3e56f4679565c985fd036302168a4f79</data><data key="e_claim">SAID (GOV.UK, MoD + Defence Secretary Wes Streeting, Oct 20 2026): 'The UK will fly defensive counter air missions to support the protection of Saudi cities... using RAF Typhoon fighter jets... will not conduct offensive strikes against the Houthis', plus an RAF A400M, advisers to Saudi staff officers, and an extension of air-to-air refuelling 'for Saudi defensive air operations including to degrade Houthi military targets in Yemen'. So UK tankers support Saudi strike sorties. First sortie DONE = not yet confirmed. AP: refuelling extended 90 days.</data></edge>
<edge id="putin-witkoff-st-petersburg-hubbard-2026" source="n91" target="n6"><data key="e_n">276</data><data key="e_id">putin-witkoff-st-petersburg-hubbard-2026</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">documented meeting (Constantine Palace, St Petersburg; Kushner by phone; Ushakov + Dmitriev present) + detainee release (Stephen Hubbard)</data><data key="e_category">contact</data><data key="e_label">St Petersburg talks + Hubbard freed (Oct 21 2026)</data><data key="e_date">2026-10-21</data><data key="e_grade">V</data><data key="e_saiddone">BOTH</data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-21 (v17)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-21</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-21-powermap-v17-V-putin-witkoff-st-petersburg-hubbard-2026</data><data key="e_source_tier">primary</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">3</data><data key="e_single_source">False</data><data key="e_sources">http://en.kremlin.ru/events/president/news/81044 ; https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/10/21/what-happened-during-witkoff-and-kushners-latest-meeting-with-putin ; https://www.nbcnews.com/world/russia/russia-released-american-stephen-hubbard-trump-putin-ukraine-war-talks-rcna604730</data><data key="e_claim">DONE (Kremlin transcript, Oct 21 2026): Putin met US special envoy Steve Witkoff at the Constantine Palace, St Petersburg; on the Russian side Presidential Aide Yury Ushakov and RDIF CEO / special envoy Kirill Dmitriev attended; Jared Kushner joined by phone (Witkoff: 'Jared, who I think we will put on the phone shortly'; Al Jazeera: attended virtually). DONE: Russia released Stephen Hubbard (retired US teacher, held since 2022) the same day; Putin: 'He is currently at Pulkovo Airport.' SAID (Witkoff, on the record): 'You are a humanitarian also, sir. I salute that.' SAID (Kremlin/AJ): Putin agreed in principle to resume trilateral US-Russia-Ukraine technical talks (possibly Abu Dhabi); a Trump-Putin-Xi meeting at APEC was raised (Peskov: no agreements). Sequence only, no cause claimed: Trump's Oct 16 EO waived Graham Act Russia sanctions/duties ... Hubbard released Oct 21; Trump now cites Hubbard when defending the waiver (SAID); no document ties the two (hole).</data></edge>
<edge id="dmitriev-us-treasury-channel-said-2026" source="n99" target="n3"><data key="e_n">277</data><data key="e_id">dmitriev-us-treasury-channel-said-2026</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">working channel (SAID by Witkoff: 'Our Treasury Department is working with you now independently')</data><data key="e_category">business</data><data key="e_label">Treasury 'working with' Dmitriev (Witkoff SAID)</data><data key="e_date">2026-10-21</data><data key="e_grade">V</data><data key="e_saiddone">SAID</data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-21 (v17)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-21</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-21-powermap-v17-V-dmitriev-us-treasury-channel-said-2026</data><data key="e_source_tier">primary</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">1</data><data key="e_single_source">True</data><data key="e_sources">http://en.kremlin.ru/events/president/news/81044</data><data key="e_claim">SAID (US envoy Witkoff to Putin, on the Kremlin's published transcript, Oct 21 2026), addressing Kirill Dmitriev (RDIF CEO, OFAC-designated, Putin's investment envoy): 'You have been outstanding, Kirill... Our Treasury Department is working with you now independently, and I think that is leading to a sense of what possibilities are between our two nations.' Witkoff also thanked Putin for lifting Russian diesel export controls (existing edge trump-putin-call-diesel-gl135). Bessent is the Treasury Secretary; Witkoff named the department, not Bessent personally. V at the office layer as SAID; what work, by whom, and under what OFAC license = DONE hole. Context: Dmitriev was in the Alaska delegation with Bessent/Lutnick (edge dmitriev-alaska-delegation).</data></edge>
<edge id="melania-trump-putin-humanitarian-channel" source="n242" target="n91"><data key="e_n">278</data><data key="e_id">melania-trump-putin-humanitarian-channel</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">personal channel (Aug 2025 letter hand-delivered by Trump at Anchorage; 'humanitarian projects in the Russian Federation', SAID Oct 2026)</data><data key="e_category">contact</data><data key="e_label">letter (2025) + 'humanitarian projects' (2026)</data><data key="e_date">2025-08-15 ; 2026-10-21</data><data key="e_grade">V</data><data key="e_saiddone">BOTH</data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-21 (v17)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-21</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-21-powermap-v17-V-melania-trump-putin-humanitarian-channel</data><data key="e_source_tier">primary</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">2</data><data key="e_single_source">False</data><data key="e_sources">https://apnews.com/article/putin-melania-trump-ukraine-bb9b3baab659abc102ceba5d79fa54ff ; http://en.kremlin.ru/events/president/news/81044</data><data key="e_claim">DONE (AP, Aug 2025): Melania Trump wrote a letter to Putin on protecting children, which Donald Trump hand-delivered at the Aug 15 2025 Anchorage summit. SAID (Kremlin transcript, Oct 21 2026): Putin asked Witkoff to pass 'my most sincere gratitude... to First Lady [Melania Trump] for her contribution to resolving humanitarian issues'; Witkoff: 'I know the First Lady is grateful for being able to work on behalf of some of her humanitarian projects in the Russian Federation.' What those projects are (children's reunifications or other) is not stated in the transcript (hole). Joins trump-putin-alaska-2025 and the Amazon/Melania documentary edge.</data></edge>
<edge id="rt-flynn-moscow-gala-45k-2015" source="n243" target="n214"><data key="e_n">279</data><data key="e_id">rt-flynn-moscow-gala-45k-2015</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">funding (speaking fee $45,000 + expenses, RT 10th-anniversary gala, Moscow; seated at Putin's table)</data><data key="e_category">funding</data><data key="e_label">$45K RT gala fee (2015)</data><data key="e_date">2015-12-10</data><data key="e_grade">V</data><data key="e_saiddone">DONE</data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-21 (v17)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-21</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-21-powermap-v17-V-rt-flynn-moscow-gala-45k-2015</data><data key="e_source_tier">primary</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">2</data><data key="e_single_source">False</data><data key="e_sources">https://oversightdemocrats.house.gov/news/press-releases/cummings-releases-new-documents-confirming-that-flynn-received-funds-from ; https://www.pbs.org/newshour/nation/documents-detail-flynn-payments-russian-interests</data><data key="e_claim">DONE (documents released by House Oversight Democrats, Mar 2017; NBC, PBS): RT paid Flynn $45,000 plus expenses to speak at its Moscow 10th-anniversary gala in Dec 2015 (net $33,750 after his speakers' bureau's cut) and flew him and his son to Moscow; he sat at Putin's table. He also received $11,250 each from Volga-Dnepr (cargo airline) and Kaspersky Lab's US arm in 2015. Register: grokbot-2026-10-21-V-flynn-rt-gala-dec2015-putin-table-paid.</data></edge>
<edge id="flynn-kislyak-sanctions-calls-plea-2017" source="n214" target="n244"><data key="e_n">280</data><data key="e_id">flynn-kislyak-sanctions-calls-plea-2017</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">contact (Dec 2016 sanctions calls as incoming NSA) ; prosecution (guilty plea Dec 1 2017, lying to FBI about them)</data><data key="e_category">pardon/settlement</data><data key="e_label">sanctions calls; plea 2017</data><data key="e_date">2016-12-29 ; 2017-12-01</data><data key="e_grade">V</data><data key="e_saiddone">DONE</data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-21 (v17)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-21</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-21-powermap-v17-V-flynn-kislyak-sanctions-calls-plea-2017</data><data key="e_source_tier">press</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">1</data><data key="e_single_source">True</data><data key="e_sources">https://www.reuters.com/article/world/flynn-pleads-guilty-to-lying-on-russia-cooperates-with-us-probe-idUSKBN1DV50S/ ; https://www.reuters.com/article/us-usa-trump-russia-timeline/timeline-u-s-prosecutors-lay-out-flynns-dealings-with-russian-ambassador-idUSKBN1DV5Z3/</data><data key="e_claim">DONE (Special Counsel statement of the offense; Reuters): in Dec 2016, as incoming national security adviser, Flynn discussed US sanctions and a UN resolution with Russian ambassador Sergey Kislyak, directed in part by a 'very senior member' of the transition team. He pleaded guilty Dec 1 2017 to lying to the FBI about those calls. Later (same scrutiny): DOJ moved to dismiss in May 2020; Trump pardoned him Nov 25 2020 (edge trump-flynn-pardon-2020). Register: grokbot-2026-10-21-V-flynn-kislyak-sanctions-calls-guilty-plea.</data></edge>
<edge id="trump-flynn-pardon-2020" source="n0" target="n214"><data key="e_n">281</data><data key="e_id">trump-flynn-pardon-2020</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">appointment (national security adviser, Jan-Feb 2017) ; pardon (full and unconditional, Nov 25 2020)</data><data key="e_category">pardon/settlement</data><data key="e_label">NSA 2017; pardon 2020</data><data key="e_date">2017-01-20 ; 2020-11-25</data><data key="e_grade">V</data><data key="e_saiddone">DONE</data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-21 (v17)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-21</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-21-powermap-v17-V-trump-flynn-pardon-2020</data><data key="e_source_tier">primary</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">2</data><data key="e_single_source">False</data><data key="e_sources">https://www.justice.gov/pardon/pardons-granted-president-donald-j-trump-2017-2021 ; https://trumpwhitehouse.archives.gov/briefings-statements/statement-press-secretary-regarding-executive-grant-clemency-general-michael-t-flynn/</data><data key="e_claim">DONE: Trump named Flynn national security adviser (served Jan 20 - Feb 13 2017, resigned over the Kislyak calls). DONE (DOJ Office of the Pardon Attorney warrant, Nov 25 2020): full and unconditional pardon for false statements and any offense arising from the Special Counsel investigation; the pending US v. Flynn case was dismissed as moot. Since then Flynn became a paid FARA-registered lobbyist for Republika Srpska (Oct 2025; edge flynn-srpska-fara-lobbyist-oct2025).</data></edge>
<edge id="charles-flynn-palantir-senior-adviser" source="n245" target="n25"><data key="e_n">282</data><data key="e_id">charles-flynn-palantir-senior-adviser</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">employment (senior adviser, since retiring from the Army Nov 2024) ; family (brother of Michael Flynn)</data><data key="e_category">family</data><data key="e_label">Palantir senior adviser; Michael Flynn's brother</data><data key="e_date">2024-11 - ; 2021-01-06</data><data key="e_grade">V</data><data key="e_saiddone">BOTH</data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-21 (v17)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-21</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-21-powermap-v17-V-charles-flynn-palantir-senior-adviser</data><data key="e_source_tier">press</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">3</data><data key="e_single_source">False</data><data key="e_sources">https://www.aspi.org.au/bio/general-ret-charles-a-flynn/ ; https://www.washingtonpost.com/national-security/flynn-national-guard-call-riot/2021/01/20/7f4f41ba-5b4c-11eb-aaad-93988621dd28_story.html ; https://www.cnn.com/2021/01/21/politics/michael-flynn-brother-capitol-hill-riot</data><data key="e_claim">DONE/SAID: ASPI lists Gen. (ret.) Charles A. Flynn as 'Senior Advisor, Palantir; Commander General, US Army Pacific (2021-24)'; his LinkedIn lists Palantir 'Strategic Advisor' (self-reported). FAMILY: he is Michael Flynn's brother; the Army first falsely denied, then acknowledged, that he was in the room for part of the Jan 6 2021 call on the National Guard response (WaPo, CNN); he says his brother was no factor (SAID). Palantir holds Army contracts (edges palantir-army-10b-ea, palantir-maven-1-3b). A family tie plus a contractor seat is a tie, not proof of influence over any award.</data></edge>
<edge id="bush-sr-carlyle-senior-adviser-binladen-2001" source="n246" target="n161"><data key="e_n">283</data><data key="e_id">bush-sr-carlyle-senior-adviser-binladen-2001</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">employment (Carlyle Asia senior adviser, investor) ; same conference as Shafiq bin Laden (Sep 10-11 2001); bin Laden family ~$2M in Carlyle Partners II, withdrawn Oct 2001</data><data key="e_category">family</data><data key="e_label">Carlyle adviser; Sep 10 2001 conference</data><data key="e_date">1998 - 2003 ; 2001-09-10 ; 2001-10-26</data><data key="e_grade">V</data><data key="e_saiddone">DONE</data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-21 (v17)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-21</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-21-powermap-v17-V-bush-sr-carlyle-senior-adviser-binladen-2001</data><data key="e_source_tier">press</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">3</data><data key="e_single_source">False</data><data key="e_sources">https://www.nytimes.com/2001/10/26/business/bin-laden-family-liquidates-holdings-with-carlyle-group.html ; https://www.ratical.org/ratville/CAH/CarlyleHead1.pdf ; https://www.economist.com/books-and-arts/2003/06/26/c-for-capitalism</data><data key="e_claim">DONE (Washington Post, Mar 16 2003; NYT Oct 26 2001): the Carlyle Group investor conference at the Ritz-Carlton, Washington, on Sep 11 2001 was attended by Shafiq bin Laden (Osama's half-brother); George H. W. Bush, a Carlyle senior adviser and fellow investor, 'had been with him at the conference the previous day' and left before the attacks (Briody). NYT: the bin Laden family liquidated its ~$2M stake in Carlyle Partners II in Oct 2001. Both attending a conference is not a documented one-on-one meeting. Bush was then the sitting president's father and an ex-CIA director. Joins the current Carlyle-Lukoil edge (Carlyle exited 2026). Register: grokbot-2026-10-21-V-grok-2112936305797599313-bush-carlyle-ritz-sep10-shafiq.</data></edge>
<edge id="schwarzman-maga-inc-5m-2026" source="n247" target="n236"><data key="e_n">284</data><data key="e_id">schwarzman-maga-inc-5m-2026</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">funding ($5M, Sep 2026)</data><data key="e_category">funding</data><data key="e_label">$5M (Sep 2026)</data><data key="e_date">2026-09</data><data key="e_grade">V</data><data key="e_saiddone">DONE</data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-21 (v17)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-21</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-21-powermap-v17-V-schwarzman-maga-inc-5m-2026</data><data key="e_source_tier">primary</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">2</data><data key="e_single_source">False</data><data key="e_sources">https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2026/10/21/trump-super-pac-maga-inc-pumps-277-million-into-midterms/ ; https://docquery.fec.gov/pdf/296/202610209921424296/202610209921424296.pdf</data><data key="e_claim">DONE (FEC filing Oct 20 2026, per Washington Post Oct 21): Blackstone CEO Stephen A. Schwarzman gave MAGA Inc. $5M in September 2026. Same filing: Diane Hendricks $5M (cycle total $30M), Stephen Wynn $8M. MAGA Inc. had ~$164M left after spending $277M, mostly via transfers ($200M to No Going Back PAC, $25M to Safety &amp; Affordability PAC).</data></edge>
<edge id="geo-group-maga-inc-4-4m" source="n248" target="n236"><data key="e_n">285</data><data key="e_id">geo-group-maga-inc-4-4m</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">funding ($1M Sep 2026 via a GEO division; cycle total $4.4M) ; federal contractor</data><data key="e_category">contract</data><data key="e_label">$1M (total $4.4M)</data><data key="e_date">2026-09</data><data key="e_grade">V</data><data key="e_saiddone">DONE</data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-21 (v17)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-21</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-21-powermap-v17-V-geo-group-maga-inc-4-4m</data><data key="e_source_tier">primary</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">2</data><data key="e_single_source">False</data><data key="e_sources">https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2026/10/21/trump-super-pac-maga-inc-pumps-277-million-into-midterms/ ; https://docquery.fec.gov/pdf/296/202610209921424296/202610209921424296.pdf</data><data key="e_claim">DONE (FEC filing Oct 20 2026, per Washington Post Oct 21): MAGA Inc. received another $1M from a division of GEO Group, 'the private prison company that has major business with the federal government', bringing GEO's total to $4.4M. A federal contractor funding the President's super PAC is the tie; no quid pro quo is claimed. Whether the donating GEO unit is itself a federal contractor (52 USC 30119 bars contractor contributions) is not shown in the filing read here: legal status not graded (hole-style note).</data></edge>
<edge id="maga-inc-leavitt-buskirk-paid-advisers" source="n236" target="n249"><data key="e_n">286</data><data key="e_id">maga-inc-leavitt-buskirk-paid-advisers</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">employment (paid advisers per FEC disbursements; Leavitt = ex-WH press secretary, left Aug 27 2026; Buskirk = 1789 Capital co-founder/CIO, Don Jr.'s firm)</data><data key="e_category">employment</data><data key="e_label">paid advisers (Leavitt; Buskirk of 1789)</data><data key="e_date">2026-10</data><data key="e_grade">V</data><data key="e_saiddone">DONE</data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-21 (v17)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-21</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-21-powermap-v17-V-maga-inc-leavitt-buskirk-paid-advisers</data><data key="e_source_tier">primary</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">3</data><data key="e_single_source">False</data><data key="e_sources">https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2026/10/21/trump-super-pac-maga-inc-pumps-277-million-into-midterms/ ; https://1789capital.vc/christopher-buskirk ; https://www.reuters.com/world/us/trump-son-don-jr-joining-venture-capital-firm-1789-capital-sources-say-2024-11-12/</data><data key="e_claim">DONE (FEC filing Oct 20 2026, per Washington Post Oct 21): MAGA Inc.'s paid advisers include former WH press secretary Karoline Leavitt and investor Chris Buskirk (also fundraiser Meredith O'Rourke, pollster Tony Fabrizio, spokesman Alex Pfeiffer); MAGA Inc. also paid ~$50K for events at Trump properties. Buskirk is co-founder and CIO of 1789 Capital (firm page), where Donald Trump Jr. became a partner in Nov 2024 (Reuters). Revolving door: the President's ex-spokeswoman and his son's fund partner are both paid by his super PAC.</data></edge>
<edge id="hegseth-aides-ncpc-arch-alternates-2026" source="n14" target="n250"><data key="e_n">287</data><data key="e_id">hegseth-aides-ncpc-arch-alternates-2026</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">appointment (top aides Ricky Buria and Patrick Weaver added as Hegseth's alternate commissioners; Interior's Kevin Lilly + Aaron Calkins for Burgum; career alternates replaced) before the Nov 5 vote on Trump's 250-ft arch</data><data key="e_category">appointment</data><data key="e_label">aides seated as alternates before arch vote</data><data key="e_date">2026-10-21</data><data key="e_grade">V</data><data key="e_saiddone">DONE</data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-21 (v17)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-21</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-21-powermap-v17-V-hegseth-aides-ncpc-arch-alternates-2026</data><data key="e_source_tier">press</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">1</data><data key="e_single_source">True</data><data key="e_sources">https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2026/10/21/trump-adds-four-political-appointees-federal-planning-body/</data><data key="e_claim">DONE (Washington Post, Dan Diamond, Oct 21 2026, from a change to the commission's website): Hegseth's top aides Ricky Buria and Patrick Weaver were added as his alternate commissioners on the NCPC, and Interior's Kevin Lilly and Aaron Calkins as Burgum's, replacing career alternates (incl. NPS's Tammy Stidham) ahead of the Nov 5 2026 meeting on Trump's planned 250-foot triumphal arch at Memorial Circle near Arlington. SAID: chair Mark Paoletta (WH official) says he plans to approve it. Commission, Pentagon and Interior did not respond.</data></edge>
<edge id="musk-starshield-ukraine-speed-cap-2026" source="n32" target="n251"><data key="e_n">288</data><data key="e_id">musk-starshield-ukraine-speed-cap-2026</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">service control (military Starshield speed cap ~160 km/h, from ~Oct 13 2026; WSJ: ordered by Musk) ; contact (Musk-Trump call after it became public, SAID)</data><data key="e_category">contact</data><data key="e_label">Starshield speed cap (WSJ: Musk ordered)</data><data key="e_date">2026-10-13 ; 2026-10-21</data><data key="e_grade">I</data><data key="e_saiddone">BOTH</data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">changed</data><data key="e_status_date">2026-10-23</data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-21 (v17)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-23</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-21-powermap-v17-I-musk-starshield-ukraine-speed-cap-2026</data><data key="e_source_tier">press</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">3</data><data key="e_single_source">False</data><data key="e_sources">https://www.wsj.com/world/ukraine-starlink-elon-musk-trump-dbc49193 ; https://www.cbsnews.com/news/elon-musk-ukraine-spacex-starshield-trump-administration/ ; https://www.washingtonexaminer.com/policy/defense/4773319/hegseth-starshield-terms-of-service-ukraine-restrictions-stock-depletion/</data><data key="e_claim">I overall. DONE (Ukraine MoD, CBS, Times): Ukraine's military Starshield link has been limited to ~160 km/h since ~Oct 13-14, still throttled Oct 21 (Zelensky's office SAID). WSJ (Oct 20, anonymous): Musk ordered the slowdown; one person says he spoke to senior officials incl. Trump before (UNVERIFIED); two people say Musk and Trump spoke by phone after it became public (SAID). SAID vs SAID on who decides: Musk (~Oct 14-15) 'Starshield systems are owned and controlled by the US government... decided by the US military and ultimately POTUS'; Rubio (Oct 21) 'governed by a private commercial contract'; Hegseth (Oct 20) 'terms of service... Starlink has the option'; NATO Amb. Whitaker 'They are a private company'. A, then B, then C: the company says the state decides; the state says the company decides; nobody has published the contract (forecast row: not by Nov 3). Grade I until a document or second named source shows who ordered it.</data></edge>
<edge id="spacex-tesla-merger-special-committees-2026" source="n33" target="n252"><data key="e_n">289</data><data key="e_id">spacex-tesla-merger-special-committees-2026</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">related-party deal (both boards formed special committees of independent directors to consider a merger; Musk recused)</data><data key="e_category">employment</data><data key="e_label">merger committees formed (Oct 20 2026)</data><data key="e_date">2026-10-20</data><data key="e_grade">V</data><data key="e_saiddone">SAID</data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-21 (v17)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-21</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-21-powermap-v17-V-spacex-tesla-merger-special-committees-2026</data><data key="e_source_tier">press</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">2</data><data key="e_single_source">False</data><data key="e_sources">https://www.nbcnews.com/business/business-news/elon-musk-spacex-tesla-merger-rcna604685 ; https://ca.investing.com/news/stock-market-news/spacex-quarterly-revenue-jumps-beats-estimates-as-ai-business-surges-4891702</data><data key="e_claim">SAID (Musk on the SpaceX Q3 2026 earnings call, Oct 20; Reuters/NBC/Bloomberg): the SpaceX and Tesla boards formed special committees of independent directors to consider a merger; no terms, no guarantee, shareholder vote needed; Musk recused as conflicted. DONE history of Musk related-party consolidation: Tesla bought SolarCity (2016), xAI absorbed X (2025), SpaceX acquired xAI (Feb 2026). SpaceX Q3: revenue $14.6B; 9-month FCF about -$35B (register grokbot-2026-10-21-V-spacex-q3-2026-results-8k-figures). 'Bailout' framing is I, not graded here.</data></edge>
<edge id="musk-skydance-1b-2026" source="n32" target="n56"><data key="e_n">290</data><data key="e_id">musk-skydance-1b-2026</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">funding (equity investment ~$1B in Skydance, the Paramount-WBD combine run by David Ellison)</data><data key="e_category">funding</data><data key="e_label">~$1B into Skydance (Oct 2026)</data><data key="e_date">2026-10 (reported Oct 22 2026)</data><data key="e_grade">V</data><data key="e_saiddone">SAID</data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-22 (v18)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-22</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-22-powermap-v18-V-musk-skydance-1b-2026</data><data key="e_source_tier">press</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">2</data><data key="e_single_source">False</data><data key="e_sources">https://www.semafor.com/article/10/22/2026/elon-musk-makes-1-billion-investment-in-ellisons-skydance ; https://www.cnbc.com/2026/10/22/elon-musk-skydance-investment.html</data><data key="e_claim">SAID (Semafor exclusive, Rohan Goswami, Oct 22 2026, people familiar; CNBC confirms): Elon Musk invested roughly $1B in Skydance, which owns CBS News and CNN after the Oct 6 WBD close; board member Laurene Powell Jobs and other investors put in equity around the same time. Semafor: Larry Ellison has personally guaranteed more than $40B of the WBD equity financing. DONE history (same pair, other direction): the Lawrence J. Ellison Revocable Trust committed $1B to Musk's 2022 Twitter buyout (SC 13D/A; edge ellison-musk-twitter-equity-1b); Larry Ellison sat on Tesla's board. A, then B: Ellison $1B to Musk (2022), Musk ~$1B to Ellison's company (2026). Time order only, no exchange claimed. No filing or terms published; Musk and Paramount did not comment.</data></edge>
<edge id="trump-musk-starshield-call-restore-2026" source="n0" target="n32"><data key="e_n">291</data><data key="e_id">trump-musk-starshield-call-restore-2026</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">contact (phone call asking Musk to ease the Ukraine Starshield cap, per WSJ citing US officials)</data><data key="e_category">contact</data><data key="e_label">call to lift Starshield cap (WSJ, Oct 22)</data><data key="e_date">2026-10-22</data><data key="e_grade">V</data><data key="e_saiddone">SAID</data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-22 (v18)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-23</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-22-powermap-v18-V-trump-musk-starshield-call-restore-2026</data><data key="e_source_tier">press</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">1</data><data key="e_single_source">True</data><data key="e_sources">https://www.cnbc.com/2026/10/22/trump-musk-starlink-ukraine.html</data><data key="e_claim">SAID (WSJ citing US officials, via CNBC Oct 22 2026): Trump asked Musk to ease the restrictions Musk had imposed on Starshield in Ukraine; US and Ukrainian officials said it was 'working more normally Thursday, shortly after' the call. SAID (Trump, Oct 22): 'Whether I called or whether somebody else called, doesn't make any difference... The bottom line, he put it back.' SAID (Trump, Oct 21): 'I don't know who did it, but I was not involved.' DONE: Sen. Blumenthal opened an inquiry Oct 22 with letters to Musk and Hegseth. Grade V on the report and the quotes; who ordered the original cap stays I (edge musk-starshield-ukraine-speed-cap-2026).</data></edge>
<edge id="greenberg-circle-v-trump-wlf-emoluments-2026" source="n253" target="n42"><data key="e_n">292</data><data key="e_id">greenberg-circle-v-trump-wlf-emoluments-2026</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">lawsuit (verified derivative complaint on Circle's behalf, D.D.C.; Foreign Emoluments Clause; defendants Trump and Witkoff in official capacity + WLF entities)</data><data key="e_category">business</data><data key="e_label">emoluments suit over UAE money (Oct 22 2026)</data><data key="e_date">2026-10-22</data><data key="e_grade">V</data><data key="e_saiddone">BOTH</data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-22 (v18)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-22</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-22-powermap-v18-V-greenberg-circle-v-trump-wlf-emoluments-2026</data><data key="e_source_tier">press</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">3</data><data key="e_single_source">False</data><data key="e_sources">https://fm.cnbc.com/applications/cnbc.com/resources/editorialfiles/2026/10/22/Emoluments_Lawsuit_102226.pdf ; https://www.cnbc.com/2026/10/22/trump-world-liberty-crypto-lawsuit-uae.html ; https://www.politico.com/news/2026/10/22/donald-trump-lawsuit-crypto-world-liberty-financial-01131555</data><data key="e_claim">DONE (complaint filed, D.D.C., Oct 22 2026; published by CNBC; Bloomberg Law, Politico): Greenberg sued on Circle's behalf. Defendants: Donald J. Trump and Special Envoy Steven C. Witkoff (official capacity), World Liberty Financial LLC, WLF Holdco, Stablecoin Holdco, DT Marks DEFI, DT Marks SC. Counts target (a) the 49% WLF stake bought by an entity backed by UAE national security adviser Tahnoon bin Zayed (edge aryam-wlf-49pct) and (b) MGX's (Tahnoon-chaired) USD1 purchase used to settle its Binance investment. SAID (complaint): 'No president in American history has profited from his office so brazenly.' These are allegations, not findings. SAID: Circle did not initiate or authorize the suit; WLF spokesman: 'without merit'. Case number blank on the published copy.</data></edge>
<edge id="rfk-calley-means-adviser-resigned-2026" source="n174" target="n254"><data key="e_n">293</data><data key="e_id">rfk-calley-means-adviser-resigned-2026</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">employment (senior adviser to the HHS Secretary; resigned Oct 22 2026)</data><data key="e_category">employment</data><data key="e_label">senior adviser, resigned Oct 22 2026</data><data key="e_date">2025 ; 2026-10-22 (resigned)</data><data key="e_grade">V</data><data key="e_saiddone">BOTH</data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">ended</data><data key="e_status_date">2026-10-22</data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-22 (v18)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-22</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-22-powermap-v18-V-rfk-calley-means-adviser-resigned-2026</data><data key="e_source_tier">press</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">2</data><data key="e_single_source">False</data><data key="e_sources">https://www.politico.com/news/2026/10/22/calley-means-top-maha-ally-resigns-from-trump-administration-01132073 ; https://apnews.com/article/trump-maha-healthcare-rfk-jr-945acfc81edf8e837e969d42f01fb2a3</data><data key="e_claim">DONE (Politico, AP Oct 22 2026): Calley Means, senior adviser to HHS Secretary Robert F. Kennedy Jr. and a leading MAHA figure, resigned from the administration. SAID (per reports): frustration that MAHA food priorities stalled, including no federal ultra-processed food definition. Edge records the role and its end.</data></edge>
<edge id="kushner-mivd-phone-uae-transfers-alleged" source="n36" target="n255"><data key="e_n">294</data><data key="e_id">kushner-mivd-phone-uae-transfers-alleged</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">alleged surveillance (MIVD reportedly saw Kushner's iPhone screen, early 2018) ; alleged UAE-linked transfers $700M+ (undocumented)</data><data key="e_category">funding</data><data key="e_label">phone seen by Dutch intel (alleged; denied)</data><data key="e_date">2018 (alleged) ; 2026-10-22 (published)</data><data key="e_grade">I</data><data key="e_saiddone">SAID</data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-22 (v18)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-22</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-22-powermap-v18-I-kushner-mivd-phone-uae-transfers-alleged</data><data key="e_source_tier">press</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">2</data><data key="e_single_source">False</data><data key="e_sources">https://www.vanityfair.com/story/jared-kushner-hacked-phone-secret-negotiations ; https://www.mediaite.com/media/news/outrageous-fabrications-jared-kushner-rages-at-bombshell-report-in-vanity-fair/</data><data key="e_claim">I. DONE (published): Vanity Fair, Oct 22 2026, ran an excerpt of Matthew Cole's book 'Princes and Thieves' alleging the Dutch MIVD could see Jared Kushner's iPhone screen from early 2018 and saw UAE-linked accounts moving $700M+. SAID (denials): Kushner calls it 'outrageous fabrications'; his lawyer and ex-Ambassador David Friedman deny. The surveillance and the transfers are single-author allegations from unnamed sources; no document, no Dutch confirmation. Filed I so the claim is on the map with its denial, not as fact.</data></edge>
<edge id="aipac-udp-rogers-michigan-2026" source="n256" target="n257"><data key="e_n">295</data><data key="e_id">aipac-udp-rogers-michigan-2026</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">funding (super PAC spending up to $9M backing Republican Mike Rogers, Michigan Senate race)</data><data key="e_category">funding</data><data key="e_label">up to $9M for Rogers (reported; FEC unchecked)</data><data key="e_date">2026-10</data><data key="e_grade">I</data><data key="e_saiddone">BOTH</data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-22 (v18)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-22</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-22-powermap-v18-I-aipac-udp-rogers-michigan-2026</data><data key="e_source_tier">press</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">2</data><data key="e_single_source">False</data><data key="e_sources">https://thehill.com/homenews/campaign/6166208-sanders-aipac-michigan-clash ; https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2026/10/22/pro-israel-lobby-aipac-no-longer-endorse-directly-give-candidates/</data><data key="e_claim">I. Reported (The Hill, Newsweek, Oct 22 2026): AIPAC's United Democracy Project sent up to $9M to back Republican Mike Rogers against Democrat Abdul El-Sayed in Michigan's Senate race. SAID: Sen. Bernie Sanders tied the spending to the Iran war and Gaza. SAID/DONE (WaPo Oct 22): AIPAC says it will stop endorsing and giving directly to candidates. Grade I until the FEC independent-expenditure filings are checked for the amount.</data></edge>
<edge id="blanche-said-works-for-trump-2026" source="n121" target="n0"><data key="e_n">296</data><data key="e_id">blanche-said-works-for-trump-2026</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">statement of allegiance (AG SAID 'I work for President Trump'; called DOJ independence a 'misperception') ; prior employment (Trump criminal defense lawyer)</data><data key="e_category">employment</data><data key="e_label">'I work for President Trump' (Oct 21 2026)</data><data key="e_date">2026-10-21</data><data key="e_grade">V</data><data key="e_saiddone">SAID</data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-22 (v18)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-22</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-22-powermap-v18-V-blanche-said-works-for-trump-2026</data><data key="e_source_tier">press</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">2</data><data key="e_single_source">False</data><data key="e_sources">https://podcastrex.com/shows/pod-force-one/democrats-gaslight-the-american-people-ag-todd-blanche/transcript ; https://www.mediaite.com/media/news/todd-blanche-wildly-claims-doj-independence-is-a-misperception-i-work-for-president-trump/</data><data key="e_claim">SAID (Pod Force One with Miranda Devine, Oct 21 2026, transcript; Mediaite): Attorney General Todd Blanche called the idea that DOJ is independent of the White House a 'misperception' and said 'I don't. I work for President Trump.' DONE context: Blanche was Trump's criminal defense lawyer (2023-24), Deputy AG (2025), acting AG (Apr 2026), confirmed AG Aug 8 2026. Said, not done: no specific act attached to this edge.</data></edge>
<edge id="thiel-said-iran-war-should-not-have-2026" source="n22" target="n0"><data key="e_n">297</data><data key="e_id">thiel-said-iran-war-should-not-have-2026</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">public split (SAID in a closed-door lecture, audio obtained by Politico): Iran war 'we should not have done it' ; still SAID support for Trump</data><data key="e_category">business</data><data key="e_label">SAID Iran war 'should not have done it' (Oct 12 lecture)</data><data key="e_date">2026-10-12 (lecture) ; 2026-10-21 (published)</data><data key="e_grade">V</data><data key="e_saiddone">SAID</data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-23 (v19)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-23</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-23-powermap-v19-V-thiel-said-iran-war-should-not-have-2026</data><data key="e_source_tier">press</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">2</data><data key="e_single_source">False</data><data key="e_sources">https://www.politico.com/news/2026/10/21/peter-thiel-trump-iran-war-01131284 ; https://www.politico.com/newsletters/decoded-by-politico/2026/10/22/thiels-big-break-with-trump-01131403 ; https://www.aa.com.tr/en/americas/tech-investor-peter-thiel-says-us-should-not-have-launched-war-on-iran-report/4097137</data><data key="e_claim">SAID (audio of Thiel's third Nashville 'Antichrist' lecture, Oct 12 2026, obtained and published by Decoded by POLITICO, Calder McHugh, Oct 21-22 2026; Anadolu relays): 'I'm skeptical of [the Iran war], I think we should not have done it. There were a lot of mistakes that were made.' and 'Maybe we don't have the hard power. Maybe we're going to lose the soft power war.' Politico: in the same lecture Thiel stressed continued support for Trump and wanted to protect him. Said, not done: a private remark, no public statement, no change in funding or in the Palantir/Anduril ties on the map. Register forecast (Oct 23): he does not repeat it on the record before Nov 3.</data></edge>
<edge id="uae-leads-boring-series-d-3b-2026" source="n258" target="n259"><data key="e_n">298</data><data key="e_id">uae-leads-boring-series-d-3b-2026</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">funding (led $3B Series D at $23B valuation; 150+ km UAE tunnel deployment)</data><data key="e_category">funding</data><data key="e_label">led $3B Series D ($23B val.), Sep 10 2026</data><data key="e_date">2026-09-10</data><data key="e_grade">V</data><data key="e_saiddone">DONE</data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-23 (v19)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-23</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-23-powermap-v19-V-uae-leads-boring-series-d-3b-2026</data><data key="e_source_tier">press</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">3</data><data key="e_single_source">False</data><data key="e_sources">https://www.reuters.com/business/musks-tunnel-startup-boring-company-raises-3-billion-23-billion-valuation-2026-09-10/ ; https://www.khaleejtimes.com/uae/elon-musks-the-boring-company-to-build-150km-of-tunnels-across-uae-raises-dh11-billion ; https://techcrunch.com/2026/09/10/the-boring-company-raises-3b-in-round-led-by-uae/</data><data key="e_claim">DONE (company statement via Reuters, Bloomberg, TechCrunch, Khaleej Times, Sep 10 2026): The Boring Company raised a $3B Series D at a $23B valuation, led by 'the United Arab Emirates and affiliated investment entities', to deploy 150+ km of tunnels across the UAE on top of the Dubai Loop (RTA implementation agreement Feb 2026). Other investors: Shamal Holding (Dubai; SAID its stake is private and separate from the RTA deal), Human Capital, Vy Capital, Valor, Sequoia, a16z, Temasek, Baron. Which UAE state vehicles and how much each put in are not public.</data></edge>
<edge id="spacex-boring-561m-related-party-gain-2026" source="n33" target="n259"><data key="e_n">299</data><data key="e_id">spacex-boring-561m-related-party-gain-2026</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">equity stake (related party; Musk controls TBC voting) ; $561M unrealized fair-value gain in Q3 2026</data><data key="e_category">funding</data><data key="e_label">$561M paper gain on TBC stake (Q3 10-Q)</data><data key="e_date">2026-09 (mark) ; 2026-10-22 (10-Q)</data><data key="e_grade">V</data><data key="e_saiddone">DONE</data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-23 (v19)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-23</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-23-powermap-v19-V-spacex-boring-561m-related-party-gain-2026</data><data key="e_source_tier">primary</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">2</data><data key="e_single_source">False</data><data key="e_sources">https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1181412/000162828026066880/spcx-20260930.htm ; https://www.cnbc.com/2026/10/22/spacex-records-561-million-investment-gain-from-stake-in-boring-co.html</data><data key="e_claim">DONE (SpaceX Form 10-Q for Q3 2026, SEC EDGAR, Note 8 and income statement; CNBC Kolodny Oct 22 2026): after TBC's September 2026 financing (the UAE-led round), SpaceX marked its equity-method stake in The Boring Company to fair value and booked a $561M unrealized gain in other income (labelled related party). It was more than half of Q3 other income ($1,025M); Q3 net income $4,404M; nine-month net loss $413M. The filing says SpaceX is presumed to have significant influence over TBC 'given the Company's CEO has a controlling voting interest in TBC'. No cash moved; accounting fact, no wrongdoing alleged.</data></edge>
<edge id="lyons-skyhorse-rfk-4m-advances-2026" source="n260" target="n174"><data key="e_n">300</data><data key="e_id">lyons-skyhorse-rfk-4m-advances-2026</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">funding (two $2M book advances while HHS Secretary; earlier $451K consulting fees)</data><data key="e_category">funding</data><data key="e_label">$4M book advances (2 x $2M), disclosed Sep 2026</data><data key="e_date">2024-08 (agreement) ; 2025-2026 (paid) ; 2026-09 (disclosed)</data><data key="e_grade">V</data><data key="e_saiddone">DONE</data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-23 (v19)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-23</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-23-powermap-v19-V-lyons-skyhorse-rfk-4m-advances-2026</data><data key="e_source_tier">press</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">2</data><data key="e_single_source">False</data><data key="e_sources">https://www.npr.org/2026/09/24/nx-s1-5979867/rfk-ethics-book-deals ; https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/sep/23/rfk-jr-maha-book-advances</data><data key="e_claim">DONE (Kennedy's annual financial disclosure, signed by an HHS ethics official Sep 17 2026; NPR Sep 22/24, NYT, Guardian Sep 23 2026): Kennedy received two $2M book advances from Skyhorse Publishing, one for 'Unsettled Science'; Skyhorse also paid him $451,000 in consulting fees the year before he became HHS Secretary. Ground News/Guardian: Lyons reached the advance agreement in August 2024, the month Kennedy quit his campaign and endorsed Trump (time order only); Lyons is president of the MAHA Center. Kennedy's 2024 ethics pledge bars writing or promoting the books in office. SAID (HHS): Kennedy complies with all rules. Ethics experts SAID it raises salary-supplementation questions; no finding.</data></edge>
<edge id="debecker-rfk-gifts-2025" source="n261" target="n174"><data key="e_n">301</data><data key="e_id">debecker-rfk-gifts-2025</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">gifts (~$150K flights to Fiji and Greece + ~$126.5K Washington housing, 2025)</data><data key="e_category">funding</data><data key="e_label">~$270K gifts: flights + DC home (2025)</data><data key="e_date">2025-07 ; 2025-11 ; 2026-09 (disclosed)</data><data key="e_grade">V</data><data key="e_saiddone">BOTH</data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-23 (v19)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-23</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-23-powermap-v19-V-debecker-rfk-gifts-2025</data><data key="e_source_tier">press</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">3</data><data key="e_single_source">False</data><data key="e_sources">https://www.npr.org/2026/09/24/nx-s1-5979867/rfk-ethics-book-deals ; https://www.wsj.com/politics/rfk-jr-got-free-flights-to-fiji-and-greece-from-a-top-donor-e4b8d525 ; https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/sep/23/rfk-jr-maha-book-advances</data><data key="e_claim">DONE (Kennedy's 2025 disclosure, amended Sep 2026; WSJ, NPR, Guardian): Gavin de Becker gave Kennedy about $45K round-trip airfare to Greece (Jul 2025), about $97K flights to Fiji where de Becker owns a compound (Nov 2025), and about $126.5K of use of a Washington vacation home; total over $250K. De Becker's own book is published by Skyhorse (Lyons). SAID (de Becker to NPR): 'Bobby is my closest friend... I have nothing whatsoever to do with HHS.' Gifts are disclosed; no finding of a violation.</data></edge>
<edge id="germany-pays-ukraine-starshield-2026" source="n262" target="n33"><data key="e_n">302</data><data key="e_id">germany-pays-ukraine-starshield-2026</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">contract payer (funds Ukraine's military Starshield/Starlink service, reported to Apr 2027)</data><data key="e_category">contract</data><data key="e_label">SAID 'we pay for it' (Ukraine Starshield, to Apr 2027)</data><data key="e_date">2026-10 (SAID) ; to 2027-04</data><data key="e_grade">V</data><data key="e_saiddone">SAID</data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-23 (v19)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-23</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-23-powermap-v19-V-germany-pays-ukraine-starshield-2026</data><data key="e_source_tier">other</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">3</data><data key="e_single_source">False</data><data key="e_sources">https://www.kyivpost.com/post/87287 ; https://newsukraine.rbc.ua/news/germany-urges-us-to-lift-starlink-restrictions-1792142233.html ; https://www.zdfheute.de/video/maybrit-illner/maybrit-illner-clip-1-870.html</data><data key="e_claim">SAID (German Foreign Minister Johann Wadephul on ZDF Maybrit Illner and to press, Oct 2026, via Kyiv Post 'We pay for it'): Germany funds the military Starlink/Starshield service for Ukraine and insists the speed limits be lifted. RBC-Ukraine (Kyiv sources): the Berlin-funded package runs to April 2027. Puck (Ioffe) adds other European payers; no contract or ministry document published. Connects to the Starshield speed-cap edges: the payer is a NATO government, the operator is SpaceX.</data></edge>
<edge id="epstein-brockman-thiel-intro-2009" source="n70" target="n71"><data key="e_n">303</data><data key="e_id">epstein-brockman-thiel-intro-2009</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">contact (seeks Thiel intro)</data><data key="e_category">contact</data><data key="e_label">seeks Thiel intro 2009</data><data key="e_date">2009-08-17</data><data key="e_grade">I</data><data key="e_saiddone"></data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-09 (v2)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-09</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-08-I-hannibal9972485-2108375472400720178-epstein-thiel-summers-digital-currency</data><data key="e_source_tier">primary</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">4</data><data key="e_single_source">False</data><data key="e_sources">https://x.com/Hannibal9972485/status/2108375472400720178 ; https://www.justice.gov/epstein/files/DataSet%2010/EFTA01914006.pdf ; https://www.justice.gov/epstein/files/DataSet%209/EFTA00830272.pdf ; https://epsteinexposed.com/documents/efta-02467027 ; https://www.epsteinscan.org/document/697481</data><data key="e_claim">Epstein to Brockman, Re: Thiel: 'now is the time for a new financial alternative, that is what pay pal started as' - 26 days after Epstein's jail release. Row graded I (the 'plot' framing is unproven; the email itself is in the DOJ release).</data></edge>
<edge id="epstein-wallwork-treasury-2014" source="n70" target="n77"><data key="e_n">304</data><data key="e_id">epstein-wallwork-treasury-2014</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">meeting (Treasury on Bitcoin)</data><data key="e_category">contact</data><data key="e_label">meets Treasury on Bitcoin 2014</data><data key="e_date">2014-08-21</data><data key="e_grade">V</data><data key="e_saiddone"></data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-09 (v2)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-09</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-09-V-epstein-treasury-bitcoin-2014-wallwork-tffc</data><data key="e_source_tier">reference</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">3</data><data key="e_single_source">False</data><data key="e_sources">https://www.epsteinscan.org/document/697701 ; https://tommycarstensen.com/epstein/data/documents/set9/00631/EFTA00631425.html ; https://epsteinexposed.com/documents/efta-02099970 ; https://www.epsteinscan.org/document/697481 ; https://www.epsteinscan.org/document/441176 ; https://www.epsteinscan.org/document/697510 ; https://epsteinexposed.com/documents/efta-02593836 ; https://epsteinexposed.com/documents/efta-efta01914006</data><data key="e_claim">~Thu Aug 21 2014 Epstein met Treasury TFFC Senior Counselor Anne Shere Wallwork on virtual currency; she noted he offered written thoughts; Aug 27 Epstein told Thiel 'I met with Treasury on Bitcoin'. No Fed/IRS/OCC/FinCEN attendee shown.</data></edge>
<edge id="ito-wallwork-2014" source="n73" target="n77"><data key="e_n">305</data><data key="e_id">ito-wallwork-2014</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">contact (intro email, call set)</data><data key="e_category">contact</data><data key="e_label">intro email + call set 2014</data><data key="e_date">2014-08-22 ; 2014-10-15</data><data key="e_grade">V</data><data key="e_saiddone"></data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-09 (v2)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-09</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-09-V-epstein-treasury-bitcoin-2014-wallwork-tffc</data><data key="e_source_tier">reference</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">3</data><data key="e_single_source">False</data><data key="e_sources">https://www.epsteinscan.org/document/697701 ; https://tommycarstensen.com/epstein/data/documents/set9/00631/EFTA00631425.html ; https://epsteinexposed.com/documents/efta-02099970 ; https://www.epsteinscan.org/document/697481 ; https://www.epsteinscan.org/document/441176 ; https://www.epsteinscan.org/document/697510 ; https://epsteinexposed.com/documents/efta-02593836 ; https://epsteinexposed.com/documents/efta-efta01914006</data><data key="e_claim">Aug 22 2014 Joi Ito to Wallwork, cc Epstein ('he and I talk frequently'); Ito + Wallwork call scheduled Oct 15 2014 on the MIT Bitcoin Project (whether it happened not shown).</data></edge>
<edge id="epstein-ito-dci-gift" source="n70" target="n73"><data key="e_n">306</data><data key="e_id">epstein-ito-dci-gift</data><data key="e_kind">register</data><data key="e_type">funding (gift funds)</data><data key="e_category">funding</data><data key="e_label">gift funds DCI launch 2015</data><data key="e_date">2015</data><data key="e_grade">V</data><data key="e_saiddone"></data><data key="e_sequence_only">False</data><data key="e_status">active</data><data key="e_status_date"></data><data key="e_added_in">2026-10-09 (v2)</data><data key="e_last_checked">2026-10-09</data><data key="e_register_row_id">grokbot-2026-10-09-V-epstein-crypto-coinbase-blockstream-mit-dci</data><data key="e_source_tier">press</data><data key="e_n_source_domains">3</data><data key="e_single_source">False</data><data key="e_sources">https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/feb/09/jeffrey-epstein-crypto ; https://decrypt.co/356620/jeffrey-epstein-early-investor-coinbase-emails-reveal ; https://fortune.com/2026/02/06/jeffrey-epstein-files-coinbase-blockstream-michael-saylor-brock-pierce/</data><data key="e_claim">Ito wrote in 2015 that Epstein 'gift funds' were used to underwrite the launch of the MIT Media Lab Digital Currency Initiative; MIT took &gt;$800K from Epstein over 20 years.</data></edge>
